cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MOLRAPTOR: Molecular Fingerprint Rapid Generator"
version: "0.4.1"
date-released: "2026-07-26"
authors:
  - family-names: "Contreras-Torres"
    given-names: "Flavio F."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2375-131X"
    affiliation: "Tecnologico de Monterrey"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NanoBiostructuresRG/molraptor"
license: "LGPL-3.0-or-later"
abstract: >-
  MOLRAPTOR is an open-source cheminformatics software package with a Python API
  and command-line interface for reproducible, SMILES-first generation of binary
  molecular fingerprints. It supports Morgan, Feature Morgan, Atom Pair,
  RDKit topological, Topological Torsion, Layered, and MACCS fingerprints
  through in-memory encoding and CSV/TXT workflows. It preserves input order
  and duplicates, isolates invalid records, and records deterministic input
  and profile hashes with runtime metadata. MOLRAPTOR parses supplied SMILES
  with RDKit but does not retrieve, curate, harmonize, canonicalize, or replace
  them.
keywords:
  - cheminformatics
  - molecular fingerprints
  - Morgan fingerprints
  - molecular representations
  - SMILES
  - RDKit
  - reproducible research
  - computational chemistry
